    {
      "title": "Trump says Super Pac will pay for taxpayer-funded ads that sparked outcry",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/05/trump-super-pac-ads",
      "description": "<p>President’s U-turn comes after Democrats and Republicans condemned use of tax dollars for pro-Trump ads</p><p>Donald Trump said on Monday he would pay for taxpayer-funded, pro-Trump ads “with money I raised for MAGA, Inc.”, a political action committee, after the television advertisements glorifying himself sparked a major backlash.</p><p>In a social media post, Trump characterized the ads, which cost at least $1.5m in federal funds, as “a positive promotion for our Great U.S.A.” and called them “a rather standard thing to do”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/05/trump-super-pac-ads\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-06T01:35:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump says taxpayers will no longer fund TV ads that praise him",
      "link": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/6/trump-says-taxpayers-will-no-longer-fund-tv-ads-that-praise-him?traffic_source=rss",
      "description": "Move comes after ethics experts criticised three nationally broadcast ads and called for independent investigations.",
      "source_name": "Al Jazeera All News",
      "published": "2026-10-06T01:51:32"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump says his super PAC will pay for taxpayer-funded ads glorifying him",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/trump-says-his-super-pac-will-pay-for-taxpayer-funded-ads-glorifying-him-126100600064_1.html",
      "description": "President Donald Trump said Monday that he will stop using taxpayer funds for television advertisements glorifying himself that sparked a major backlash, and instead tap his super PAC to cover costs going forward.\nIn a post on his social media site, Trump defended the ads, which cost at least USD 1.5 million in federal funds and have drawn intense criticism. Trump said they were \"positive promotion for our Great USA.\"\n\"This is a rather standard thing to do,\" the president wrote, while blaming intense criticism for using taxpayer funds on the ads on the \"Radical Left.\" But the president added that he'd \"decided to do the Patriotic Ads, among others, and pay for them myself, and with money I raised for MAGA, Inc.\"\nThat is Trump's political war chest, which had amassed more than USD 400 million by the end of July. Trump has begun to tap it to boost Republican candidates around the country ahead of midterm elections.\nTrump provided no details on reimbursing taxpayers for ads that alrea",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-06T02:55:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump says MAGA Inc. PAC will pay for controversial TV ads that government funded",
